# Test Sections — {{ project_name }}

Living cache of section/folder paths in **{{ test_repo_label }}**. Written back by
bdd-agent after creating a new section. Agents read this before creating cases so they
place them in the correct location without a live API query.

## Format

Each row maps a feature module path to its section ID in {{ test_repo_label }}.

| Module path | Section ID | {{ test_repo_label }} path | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `<domain>/<feature>` | `<SECTION_ID>` | `<Full path in {{ test_repo_label }}>` | Created for ticket `<ticket-key>` |

## How to Use

### Reading (before creating cases)

1. Look up the feature's module path in this table.
2. If a match exists, use that section ID — do not create a duplicate.
3. If no match exists, determine the correct parent section from the module hierarchy,
   create the new section in {{ test_repo_label }}, then add a row here.

### Writing (after bdd-agent creates a section)

Append a row with the exact section ID returned by {{ test_repo_label }}:

```
| `<domain>/<feature>` | `<SECTION_ID>` | `<Full path>` | Created for `<ticket-key>` |
```

Commit this file to the branch (do not push to main — the PR includes this update).

## Section Hierarchy

Document the module hierarchy that mirrors your {{ test_repo_label }} folder structure:

```
{{ project_name }}
├── <domain-1>/
│   ├── <feature-a>/
│   └── <feature-b>/
└── <domain-2>/
    └── <feature-c>/
```

Update this tree as new sections are created.

## Notes

- Never delete a row — deprecated sections get a `[deprecated]` note in the Notes column.
- The `Module path` column uses forward slashes regardless of the test repo's folder separator.
- If {{ test_repo_label }} returns a string ID (e.g. `feat-123`), record it verbatim.
{% if test_repo == 'testrail' %}
- TestRail section IDs are numeric — record the raw integer.
{% endif %}
